title: Federal Committee: the red lines
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: red_lines_seen = 0 and elections_held >= 1 and morning_seen = 1 and year = 2015
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: red_lines_seen = 1

= 28 December 2015 — The Federal Committee

The regional barons arrive at Ferraz with a resolution already drafted. The PSOE will not negotiate with any party that supports a self-determination referendum for Catalonia, and Sánchez must bring any agreement back to the Federal Committee.

Susana Díaz's allies call it a guarantee of the party's identity. Your team calls it a cage.

- @accept: Accept the red lines as written
- @soften: Accept the principle, but negotiate the wording
- @defy: Refuse: the leadership must be free to negotiate

@accept
on-arrival: red_lines = 1; regional_leaders_dissent -= 10; institutionalists_dissent -= 5; sanchez_authority -= 5; federal_committee_balance -= 3

The barons are satisfied. Talks with ERC and Convergència are now off the table, and everyone knows who wrote the rules.

@soften
on-arrival: red_lines = 1; regional_leaders_dissent += 3; sanchez_authority += 2; member_morale += 2

The final text bars any referendum, but leaves you to decide which parties you talk to. It is a draw, and both sides claim it.

@defy
on-arrival: populism += 1; red_lines = 0; regional_leaders_dissent += 20; institutionalists_dissent += 10; federal_committee_balance -= 8; sanchez_authority += 4; member_morale += 4

The vote is close. You keep your freedom to negotiate, but Susana Díaz has counted her votes, and so have you.

@iglesias_offer
title: Iglesias's offer
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: year = 2016 and month >= 1 and month <= 3 and acting = 1 and psoe_in_government = 0 and rel_up >= 25 and formation_weeks >= 3 and sanchez_leader = 1
max-visits: 1

= Pablo Iglesias makes an offer

Leaving his audience with the King, Pablo Iglesias announces to the press that he is offering the PSOE a coalition government: Sánchez as Prime Minister, Iglesias as Vice-President, and Podemos ministers in key portfolios. You learn of it from the television.

- @welcome: Welcome the offer and invite Podemos to formal talks
- @programme: Say talks must start from the programme, not from posts
- @reject: Reject it publicly as an ultimatum

@welcome
on-arrival: rel_up += 10; up_talks += 1; progressives_dissent -= 6; regional_leaders_dissent += 10; institutionalists_dissent += 6; rel_cs -= 6

Podemos claims the initiative. Your barons say you have been humiliated in public and thanked Iglesias for it.

@programme
on-arrival: rel_up += 3; sanchez_authority += 3; regional_leaders_dissent += 2

You keep the door open without walking through it on Iglesias's terms. The commentators call it a good afternoon's work.

@reject
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_up -= 12; Q.rel_cs += 5; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 6; Q.progressives_dissent += 8; Q.member_morale -= 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', 'up', {students: 1, workers: 0.5}); } !}

The barons applaud. Many members, who voted for change, do not.

@pp_round
title: The King's consultations
new-page: true
face-image: img/spain/event_rajoy_sanchez.jpg
tags: sp_event
view-if: acting = 1 and pp_asked < formation_round and election_year = 0 and investiture_votes = 0 and formation_weeks >= 2 and psoe_largest = 0 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: {! Q.pp_asked = Q.formation_round || 1; !}

= [+ right_leader +] asks for support

The King has finished his consultations and offered the nomination to [+ right_leader +], the leader of the largest party of the right. Before deciding whether to accept, [+ right_leader +] calls you. [? if right_is_cs = 1 : Ciudadanos has overtaken the PP; Rivera offers a government of Ciudadanos and the PP, ?][? if right_is_cs = 0 : Rajoy wants the PSOE to let him govern, ?] with your vote in favour, or at least an abstention. Many of the PSOE's voters, and most of its younger ones, will never forgive a PSOE that hands the right another term.

What will the PSOE do?

- @against: Vote against [+ right_leader +]
- @abstain: Abstain and let a PP government be formed
- @limited: Negotiate a limited agreement in exchange for abstention
- @other_candidate: Demand a different PP candidate
- @grand: Offer the PP a grand coalition
- @grand_early: Offer the PP a grand coalition

@against
on-arrival: {! Q.psoe_stance_pp = "no"; Q.member_morale += 4; Q.rel_pp -= 6; Q.sanchez_authority += 2; if ((Q.fatigue || 0) >= 1 && !Q.psoe_largest && !Q.rebellion_used && !Q.third_election_threat) { Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 10; Q.third_election_threat = 1; Q.threat_week = Math.max((Q.formation_weeks || 0) + 4, 10); } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'up', 'psoe', {workers: 1, students: 1}); } !}
go-to: pp_decides

@abstain
on-arrival: {! Q.psoe_stance_pp = "abstain"; Q.member_morale -= 15; Q.progressives_dissent += 20; Q.trade_unionists_dissent += 10; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 8; Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 6; Q.rel_pp += 10; Q.sanchez_authority -= 10; Q.sanchismo -= 5; Q.progressives_strength -= 5; Q.abstained_for_pp = 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', {up: 0.85, iu: 0.15}, {workers: 5, students: 5, unemployed: 4, professionals: 3, pensioners: 1}); } !}
go-to: pp_decides

@limited
on-arrival: {! Q.psoe_stance_pp = "abstain"; Q.member_morale -= 10; Q.progressives_dissent += 12; Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 4; Q.rel_pp += 6; Q.sanchez_authority -= 5; Q.progressives_strength -= 2; Q.abstained_for_pp = 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', {up: 0.85, iu: 0.15}, {workers: 2.5, students: 2.5, unemployed: 2, professionals: 1.5}); } !}
go-to: pp_decides

@grand
view-if: grand_possible = 1 and right_is_cs = 0 and vox_on = 1
subtitle: Stable government and a veto on Vox; the PSOE's left and the unions revolt. Podemos gains, Vox gains far more as the only opposition on the right, and both keep gaining while it lasts
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.grandCoalitionOffer(Q); } !}
go-to: grand_yes if grand_accepted = 1; grand_no if grand_accepted = 0

@grand_early
view-if: grand_possible = 1 and right_is_cs = 0 and vox_on = 0
subtitle: Stable government; the PSOE's left and the unions revolt. Podemos gains on the left, Ciudadanos and abstention on the right, and the bleeding goes on while it lasts
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.grandCoalitionOffer(Q); } !}
go-to: grand_yes if grand_accepted = 1; grand_no if grand_accepted = 0

@grand_yes
title: A grand coalition

= A grand coalition

[+ pp_leader +] accepts. For the first time, the PP and the PSOE will govern together: [+ pp_leader +] as Prime Minister, Pedro Sánchez as Deputy Prime Minister, the PSOE with a share of the ministries. The barons and the institutions are relieved. Your progressives call it a betrayal, the UGT and CCOO are furious, and Podemos opens its doors to every disappointed socialist.

[? if grand_vox = 1 : On the right, the coalition shuts Vox out of power for the whole legislature. Santiago Abascal calls it "the PSOE-PP" and says only Vox is left to oppose the left. The PP's hard-liners are already listening, and so are some of Ciudadanos's voters and your own in the working-class suburbs. ?][? if grand_vox = 0 : On the right, the PP's hard-liners call it a surrender to the socialists. Some say they will vote for Ciudadanos next time, others that they will not vote at all. ?]

@grand_no
title: The PP says no

= The PP says no

[+ pp_leader +] thanks you for the offer and declines it. The PP prefers to govern with partners closer to its own ideas.

- @against: Vote against [+ right_leader +]
- @abstain: Abstain and let a PP government be formed

@other_candidate
on-arrival: {! Q.psoe_stance_pp = "no"; Q.rel_pp -= 10; Q.sanchez_authority += 3; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 3; !}
go-to: pp_decides

@pp_decides
on-arrival: {!
if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.SpainParliament) {
    var cand = Q.right_candidate || 'pp';
    var v = window.SpainParliament.investiture(Q.congress, cand, Q);
    if (v.passes) {
        Q.psoe_voted_no = Q.psoe_stance_pp === 'abstain' ? 0 : 1;
        window.SpainGame.holdInvestiture(Q, cand);
        Q.pp_invested_now = 1;
    } else {
        Q.pp_invested_now = 0;
        Q.rajoy_declined = 1;
    }
}
!}
go-to: pp_invested if pp_invested_now = 1; pp_declines if pp_invested_now = 0

@pp_invested
title: A government of the right

= A government of the right

[? if psoe_voted_no = 0 : With the PSOE's abstention, [+ right_leader +] is invested Prime Minister: [+ government_type +]. The country has a government. In the PSOE, the argument about who allowed it has only begun. Membership cards are torn up on social media, and the polls show left-wing voters moving to Podemos. ?][? if psoe_voted_no = 1 : The PSOE votes no, but the right has the votes without it: [+ right_leader +] is invested Prime Minister, [+ government_type +]. Your "no" changed nothing in the chamber; in Ferraz, the critics say a party that cannot block a government cannot lead one either. ?]

@pp_declines
title: The right's candidate declines

= [+ right_leader +] declines the nomination

Without the votes, [+ right_leader +] does something no candidate had done before: declines the King's offer, and waits for others to fail. The initiative passes to you, if you want it.

- @offer: Tell the King you are ready to seek the investiture
- @hold: Hold back and keep negotiating

@offer
on-arrival: sanchez_nominated = 1; sanchez_authority += 5; member_morale += 4

The King proposes you as candidate. The Speaker will set the date of the debate when you are ready. (Use the "Seek investiture" card.)

@hold
on-arrival: sanchez_authority -= 2

You tell the King you need more time. [+ right_leader +]'s strategy depends on everyone else's patience running out first.

@king_turns
title: The King turns to you
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: rajoy_declined = 1 and sanchez_nominated = 0 and investiture_votes = 0 and acting = 1 and election_year = 0 and king_asked < formation_round and formation_weeks >= 5 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: {! Q.king_asked = Q.formation_round || 1; !}

= The King turns to you

After a second round of consultations, the King asks whether you will stand. If no one does, the investiture clock never starts and the country stays in limbo.

- @king_accept: Accept the nomination
- @king_refuse: Refuse: [+ right_leader +] must face the chamber first

@king_accept
on-arrival: sanchez_nominated = 1; sanchez_authority += 4

You are the candidate. (Use the "Seek investiture" card when you are ready.)

@king_refuse
on-arrival: {!
if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.SpainGame) {
    window.SpainGame.holdInvestiture(Q, Q.right_candidate || 'pp');
}
Q.sanchez_authority -= 3;
!}

The King proposes [+ right_leader +], who this time goes to the vote and loses it. The two-month clock has started: if no one is invested, Spain votes again.

