    Q.regions['Cataluña'].lastWasSnap = true;
}
!}

= Mas calls a "plebiscitary" election

Artur Mas calls Catalan elections for 27 September and declares them a plebiscite on independence. His Convergència and its rival ERC will run on a single list, Junts pel Sí. If it wins a majority, they promise to start the road to independence.

- @psc_federal: The PSC campaigns for a federal Spain and a negotiated reform
- @unionist_front: Join a common front of the parties against independence
- @psc_alone: Leave the campaign to the PSC

@psc_federal
on-arrival: {! Q.cat_dialogue += 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'psoe', 1.03); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } !}

Iceta's dancing becomes the image of the campaign. The PSC holds its ground better than feared.

@unionist_front
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_cs += 4; Q.rel_pp += 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'cs', 1.05); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } !}

The front against independence has a leader, and it is Inés Arrimadas of Ciudadanos, not the PSC.

@psc_alone
on-arrival: sanchez_authority -= 1

The PSC fights alone.

@dissolution_2015
title: Rajoy dissolves the Cortes
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: legislature_expired = 1 and elections_held = 0 and campaign_line = 0
on-arrival: dissolution_2015_seen = 1

= Rajoy dissolves the Cortes

Mariano Rajoy has run his legislature to the end. He signs the dissolution of the Cortes and calls the general election for [+ election_month : month +] [+ election_year +], the last possible date.

He goes to the country on the economy: Spain is growing again, and unemployment is falling, if from 26% to 21%. Against him: four years of austerity and cuts to health and education; the labour reform; Bárcenas's accounts and the Gürtel trials; the black cards and Púnica; the 2012 bank bailout. The PP still leads the polls, but a long way below the 44.6% that gave it its majority. The majority itself is gone: the question is who will govern without one.

Four parties can now win more than 10%. What line does the PSOE take into the campaign?

- @change: Change: no deals with Rajoy, a government of progress
- @governing: A governing party: serious, moderate, ready from day one
- @vs_podemos: The only real alternative: Podemos is a risk Spain cannot take

@change
on-arrival: {!
Q.campaign_line = 1; Q.rel_pp -= 8; Q.rel_up += 6; Q.member_morale += 5; Q.progressives_dissent -= 5;
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {workers: 1.5, students: 1.5, unemployed: 1}); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); }
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0.5, 0); }
!}

You promise that the PSOE will never make Rajoy Prime Minister. It energises the members and closes a door you may later want open.

@governing
on-arrival: {!
Q.campaign_line = 2; Q.rel_cs += 6; Q.rel_pnv += 3; Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 5; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 4;
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {pensioners: 1.5, professionals: 1, self_employed: 0.5}); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); }
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -0.5, 0); }
!}

The barons approve. Older and middle-class voters hear a party of government; younger ones hear the past.

@vs_podemos
on-arrival: {!
Q.campaign_line = 3; Q.rel_up -= 12; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 6; Q.progressives_dissent += 5;
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {pensioners: 2, homemakers: 1.5, students: -1}); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); }
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -0.5, 0); }
!}

Your attacks on Iglesias hold the PSOE's older voters. Podemos will remember them when the talking starts.

@finance_crisis
title: The treasurer's report
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: deep_debt = 1 and sanchez_leader = 1 and finance_crisis_year < year
on-arrival: {! Q.finance_crisis_year = Q.year; !}

= The treasurer's report

The party treasurer brings the Federal Executive a report it cannot ignore: the PSOE owes [+ funds_display +] in party funds' worth to banks and suppliers, staff are being paid late, and the federations are asking where their money has gone. Your critics are already saying that a man who cannot run the party's accounts cannot run the country's.

- @cut_staff: Cut Ferraz's staff and campaign budget
- @appeal_members: Appeal to the members for an emergency contribution
- @blame_predecessors: Blame the debts inherited from the previous leadership

@cut_staff
on-arrival: funds += 3; sanchismo -= 6; member_morale -= 4; modernisers_dissent += 6

Dozens of party staff are let go, many of them your own people. The books improve; the loyalty of your team does not.

@appeal_members
on-arrival: funds += 2; member_morale -= 6; sanchez_authority -= 3

The members pay, and some of them ask why they have to.

@blame_predecessors
on-arrival: sanchez_authority -= 4; institutionalists_dissent += 10; regional_leaders_dissent += 6; federal_committee_balance -= 6

The old guard takes it personally. The debts are still there.

@finance_ouster
title: Removed over the finances
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: ruinous_debt = 1 and sanchez_leader = 1 and federal_committee_balance < 55
on-arrival: {!
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.oust(Q, false); }
!}

= Removed over the finances

With the party unable to pay its own campaign debts, the Federal Committee meets in emergency session. The regional barons, the old guard and even some of your own executive vote to remove you for "the ruinous management of the party". A caretaker committee takes over Ferraz.

[? if leadership_exception_open = 1 : The members have not spoken yet. The next primary is due in May 2017. ?]

@cat_155_gov
title: Independence declared
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: catalan_crisis = 1 and cat_crisis_stage = 2 and time >= cat_stage_time + 1 and psoe_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {! Q.cat_crisis_stage = 3; !}

= Independence declared

The Parliament of Catalonia votes a declaration of independence. The decision is yours: as Prime Minister, only you can ask the Senate to authorise Article 155, and the PP's majority there will grant it. [? if depends_on_catalans = 1 : Your government survives on the votes of the very parties that have just declared independence. ?]

- @gov_155_elections: Apply Article 155 and call Catalan elections at once
- @gov_155_long: Apply Article 155 indefinitely, until order is restored
- @gov_no_155: Refuse Article 155: negotiate with the Generalitat

@gov_155_elections
on-arrival: {!
Q.rel_pp += 8; Q.rel_cs += 8; Q.rel_erc -= 20; Q.rel_junts -= 25; Q.rel_up -= 6; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 10; Q.progressives_dissent += 6; Q.cat_hard_line += 1;
if (Q.regions && Q.regions['Cataluña']) { var y = Q.year, m = Q.month + 2; if (m > 12) { m -= 12; y += 1; } Q.regions['Cataluña'].nextElection = y + '-' + (m < 10 ? '0' : '') + m + '-21'; Q.regions['Cataluña'].lastWasSnap = true; }
if (Q.depends_on_catalans) { Q.depends_on_catalans = 0; Q.lost_majority = 1; }
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {pensioners: 1.5, homemakers: 1, self_employed: 0.5}); window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'psoe', 0.97); window.SpainGame.partyRel(Q, 'erc', 'up', -5); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, -1); }
!}

The Catalan government is dismissed and elections are called. Most of Spain backs you; the PSC holds its own. [? if lost_majority = 1 : ERC and Junts will never vote with you again: your government no longer has a majority. ?]

@gov_155_long
on-arrival: {!
Q.rel_pp += 10; Q.rel_cs += 10; Q.rel_erc -= 30; Q.rel_junts -= 30; Q.rel_up -= 15; Q.rel_pnv -= 10; Q.progressives_dissent += 15; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 12; Q.cat_hard_line += 2;
if (Q.regions && Q.regions['Cataluña']) { var y = Q.year + 1, m = Q.month; Q.regions['Cataluña'].nextElection = y + '-' + (m < 10 ? '0' : '') + m + '-21'; Q.regions['Cataluña'].lastWasSnap = true; }
if (Q.depends_on_catalans) { Q.depends_on_catalans = 0; Q.lost_majority = 1; }
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {pensioners: 2, homemakers: 1.5}); window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', 'up', {students: 1.5, workers: 1}); window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'psoe', 0.92); window.SpainGame.territorial(Q, 'Cataluña', 'erc', 1.1); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, -2); }
!}

Direct rule from Madrid for a year. The State is in control; in Catalonia, the independence movement has never been stronger, and the PNV is alarmed.

@gov_no_155
on-arrival: {!
Q.rel_pp -= 20; Q.rel_cs -= 25; Q.rel_erc += 10; Q.rel_junts += 10; Q.rel_up += 6; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 35; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 20; Q.federal_committee_balance -= 15; Q.sanchez_authority -= 10; Q.cat_dialogue += 2;
if (Q.regions && Q.regions['Cataluña']) { var y = Q.year, m = Q.month + 4; if (m > 12) { m -= 12; y += 1; } Q.regions['Cataluña'].nextElection = y + '-' + (m < 10 ? '0' : '') + m + '-21'; Q.regions['Cataluña'].lastWasSnap = true; }
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', {pp: 0.4, cs: 0.4, vox: 0.2}, {pensioners: 3, homemakers: 2.5, self_employed: 2, workers: 1.5, professionals: 1}); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'vox', {pensioners: 2, self_employed: 2, workers: 1.5}); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 3); }
!}

You refuse to suspend autonomy and open talks. The PP and Ciudadanos call it treason and fill the streets of Madrid; the barons openly discuss replacing you. The Generalitat agrees to new Catalan elections in four months.

@partners_price
title: Your partners' price
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: catalan_crisis = 1 and psoe_in_government = 1 and depends_on_catalans = 1 and partners_price_seen = 0
on-arrival: partners_price_seen = 1

= Your partners' price

ERC and Junts remind you that your government exists because of their votes. Their price for keeping it alive: a negotiation on a self-determination referendum, and the release of the jailed independence leaders.

- @concede_talks: Open talks that include their demands
- @dialogue_only: A dialogue table, but no referendum
- @refuse_partners: Refuse: you will not negotiate the unity of Spain

@concede_talks
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_erc += 15; Q.rel_junts += 15; Q.cat_dialogue += 2; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 25; Q.rel_cs -= 20; Q.rel_pp -= 15; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', {pp: 0.4, cs: 0.35, vox: 0.25}, {pensioners: 2.5, homemakers: 2, self_employed: 1.5, workers: 1}); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 2.5); window.SpainGame.partyRel(Q, 'cs', 'pp', 10); } !}

Your majority survives. Ciudadanos and the PP accuse you of selling Spain; across the country, moderates are listening to them.

@dialogue_only
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_erc += 5; Q.rel_junts -= 5; Q.cat_dialogue += 1; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 8; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', {pp: 0.5, cs: 0.5}, {pensioners: 1, homemakers: 1}); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 1); } !}

ERC accepts the table, for now. Junts calls it a trap. Your majority hangs on ERC's patience.

@refuse_partners
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_erc -= 20; Q.rel_junts -= 20; Q.depends_on_catalans = 0; Q.lost_majority = 1; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 10; Q.sanchez_authority += 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {pensioners: 1.5, homemakers: 1}); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, -1); } !}

The country's majority applauds. In Congress, you no longer have one: every vote from now on is a negotiation.

@king_nominates_psoe
title: The King nominates you
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: acting = 1 and psoe_largest = 1 and pp_asked < formation_round and election_year = 0 and investiture_votes = 0 and formation_weeks >= 2 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: {! Q.pp_asked = Q.formation_round || 1; Q.sanchez_nominated = 1; Q.sanchez_authority += 5; Q.member_morale += 5; !}

= The King nominates you

The PSOE is the largest party in Congress. After his consultations, the King proposes you as candidate for President of the Government. The right will vote against; everything depends on the deals you can strike. (Use the "Seek investiture" card when you are ready.)

@king_second_round
title: The King's second round
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: acting = 1 and right_failed_vote = 1 and investiture_clock > 0 and sanchez_nominated = 0 and sanchez_leader = 1 and election_year = 0 and king_second_asked < formation_round
on-arrival: {! Q.king_second_asked = Q.formation_round || 1; !}

= The King's second round

[+ right_leader +] has lost the vote in Congress. The two-month clock is running. The King calls a new round of consultations and asks whether you can find the votes.

- @second_accept: Accept the nomination and seek a majority
- @second_refuse: Decline: let the clock run out

@second_accept
on-arrival: sanchez_nominated = 1; sanchez_authority += 3

You are the candidate. (Use the "Seek investiture" card when your partners are ready.)

@second_refuse
on-arrival: sanchez_authority -= 2

The clock keeps running towards a new election.

@final_campaign
title: The final campaign
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: general_election_due = 1 and final_campaign_round <= elections_held and sanchez_active = 1
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame && !Q.eday) { window.SpainGame.startFinalCampaign(Q); } !}

= The final campaign

Polling day is close. Whatever money is left can buy one last push: rallies and adverts in a region, a message aimed at one group, or attack ads against a rival. It moves votes on election day; little of it lasts beyond.

Last-minute money buys little: the airtime is booked, the message is set and most voters have made up their minds. A spend now does about half of what the same money did during the legislature, repeating one halves it again, and every unit already spent this campaign makes the next one weaker.

Party funds: **[+ funds_display +]**. Spent so far: [+ eday_spent +].

[? if eday_spent > 0 : A new spend now does [+ eday_next_factor +]% of what the first one did. ?]

[+ my_party_cap +] on election day, on current spending: **[+ eday_poll +]%** (without the final push: [+ eday_base_poll +]%), about [+ eday_seats +] seats.

[? if eday_spent > 0 : [+ eday_last +] ?]

- @fc_class: Target a group
- @fc_region: Concentrate on a region
- @fc_attack: Run attack ads
- @fc_go: Go to the polls

@fc_go
on-arrival: {! Q.final_campaign_round = (Q.elections_held || 0) + 1; !}

The campaign closes at midnight on Friday. Saturday is the day of reflection.

