@deadlock_broken
title: No third election
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: deadlock_broken = 1
on-arrival: deadlock_broken = 0

= No third election

On the eve of a second dissolution, with the country facing a third election in a row, [+ deadlock_by +] gives in: its deputies abstain in one last investiture vote. [+ pm +] is invested: [+ government_type +]. [? if sanchez_pm = 0 : [? if sanchez_leader = 1 : [? if group_defied = 1 : You ordered the group to vote no. The barons' deputies abstained anyway: the PSOE group has defied its own Secretary-General in public. ?] The PSOE's members feel betrayed by their own deputies, and Podemos opens its doors to every disappointed socialist. ?] ?][? if sanchez_pm = 1 : The PP calls it a sacrifice for Spain. You call it the voters' verdict. ?]

@censure_budget
title: The budget vote
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: sanchez_pm = 1 and censure_budget_seen = 0 and censure_time > 0 and time >= censure_time + 9 and budget_passed = 0 and election_year = 0
on-arrival: {! Q.censure_budget_seen = 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.holdBudget(Q); } if (!Q.budget_passed) { Q.sanchez_authority -= 4; } else { Q.budget_year = Q.year; Q.sanchez_authority += 8; } !}

= The budget vote

A government born of a motion of no confidence has to pass a budget of its own, or admit it cannot govern. María Jesús Montero presents the accounts; the Catalan independence parties, with their leaders on trial, decide their fate.

{!<div class="sp-last-vote"></div>!}

Yes [+ inv_yes +], no [+ inv_no +]. [? if budget_passed = 1 : The budget passes. The legislature can run its course. ?][? if budget_passed = 0 : The budget is defeated. ERC and Junts have voted with the PP, Ciudadanos and Vox. ?]

- @cb_snap: Call an early general election [? if budget_passed = 0 : (the voters can give you the majority this Congress will not) ?]
- @cb_carry: Govern on with the rolled-over budget
- @cb_fine: Continue

@cb_snap
view-if: budget_passed = 0
subtitle: An election in two months, while the right is divided and you hold the office
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.callElection(Q); } Q.member_morale += 3; !}

You announce the dissolution of the Cortes. Spain votes in two months.

@cb_carry
view-if: budget_passed = 0
subtitle: Keeps you in office; every month without a budget wears the government down
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority -= 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.econ(Q, -0.1, 0); } !}

You govern by decree where you can and by patience where you cannot.

@cb_fine
view-if: budget_passed = 1

@diaz_snap_2018
title: Díaz calls an election
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: diaz_snap18_seen = 0 and year = 2018 and month >= 10 and regions_andalucia_psoe = 1
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.diaz_snap18_seen = 1;
if (Q.regions && Q.regions['Andalucía']) {
    Q.regions['Andalucía'].nextElection = '2018-12-02';
    Q.regions['Andalucía'].lastWasSnap = true;
}
!}

= Díaz calls an election

Susana Díaz calls an Andalusian election for 2 December, months early. Her pact with Ciudadanos has run its course, and she would rather face the voters before a general election than after one. In Ferraz, some suspect she also wants a strong result to measure against yours.

- @diaz18_campaign: Campaign at her side: a socialist Andalusia is a socialist Spain
- @diaz18_distance: Let her run her own campaign

@diaz18_campaign
subtitle: Costs 1 in party funds; her result becomes your result, good or bad
on-arrival: {! Q.funds -= 1; Q.diaz_relation += 5; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Andalucía', 'psoe', 1.02); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } !}

You share her stages. The old rivals smile for the cameras.

@diaz18_distance
subtitle: Keeps your distance from her result
on-arrival: {! Q.diaz_relation -= 3; !}

Andalusia is Susana's campaign.

@lopez_offer
title: Patxi López calls
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: leadership_exception_open = 1 and lopez_decided = 0 and sanchez_moderniser = 1 and calendar_seen = 1 and (year >= 2017)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {! Q.lopez_decided = 1; Q.lopez_announce_time = Q.time; Q.lopez_conditional = Math.random() < 0.6 ? 1 : 0; Q.lopez_endorses = Q.lopez_conditional ? 0 : 1; !}

= Patxi López calls

Patxi López was going to run as the candidate between you and Susana Díaz. But you have spent the months since Ferraz talking about a modern, reforming party, and that is his ground. He will not run against you.

[? if lopez_conditional = 0 : He will endorse you, without conditions: "The party needs to move forward, and Pedro is the one who can take it there." ?][? if lopez_conditional = 1 : He will endorse you, on two conditions: a federal party in which the federations have a real say, and a senior post in your Executive for him. ?]

Not everyone is pleased. José Antonio Pérez Tapias, of Izquierda Socialista, announces that he will run: if you are now the modernisers' candidate, someone has to stand for the left.

- @lopez_thanks: Thank him and welcome his support
- @lopez_accept: Accept his conditions
- @lopez_refuse: Refuse: you will not trade posts for endorsements

@lopez_thanks
view-if: lopez_conditional = 0
on-arrival: {! Q.modernisers_dissent -= 4; !}

He stands beside you at your next rally in Bilbao.

@lopez_accept
view-if: lopez_conditional = 1
subtitle: López's endorsement brings most of his voters; the federations will hold you to the promise, and your left resents the deal
on-arrival: {! Q.lopez_endorses = 1; Q.federal_promise = (Q.federal_promise || 0) + 1; Q.modernisers_dissent -= 4; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 2; Q.progressives_dissent += 3; Q.lopez_post = 1; !}

The deal is done in a hotel in Madrid. López will campaign for you.

@lopez_refuse
view-if: lopez_conditional = 1
subtitle: Keeps your hands free; López stays out of the race but backs no one, and his voters scatter
on-arrival: {! Q.lopez_endorses = 0; Q.sanchismo += 2; Q.modernisers_dissent += 3; !}

"Then I will stay out of it," López says. He does.

@diaz_courts
title: Susana Díaz holds court
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: leadership_exception_open = 1 and diaz_courts_seen = 0 and ((year = 2016 and month >= 11) or year >= 2017)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: diaz_courts_seen = 1

= Susana Díaz holds court

On 17 November Susana Díaz shares a stage with Felipe González; on 16 December, with José Luis Rodríguez Zapatero. She has not said she will run. She does not need to: two former prime ministers and most of the regional barons are standing beside her, and the photographs say the rest.

- @courts_halls: Answer from the local branches: "the party belongs to its members"
- @courts_attack: Attack the old guard: "the PSOE of the IBEX"
- @courts_quiet: Say nothing for now

@courts_halls
subtitle: Builds your network; no new enemies
on-arrival: {! Q.network = (Q.network || 0) + 5; Q.sanchismo += 3; !}

While she poses with ex-presidents, you sit in a hall in Xàtiva with sixty members.

@courts_attack
subtitle: Your followers love it; the regional barons and the old guard close ranks against you
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchismo += 6; Q.populism += 1; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 6; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 6; !}

"They have the former presidents; we have the members." The line is everywhere by the evening.

@courts_quiet
on-arrival: {! Q.member_morale -= 1; !}

The season of photographs is hers.

@gestora_calendar
title: The caretaker committee sets the date
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: leadership_exception_open = 1 and calendar_seen = 0 and year >= 2017
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: calendar_seen = 1

= The caretaker committee sets the date

[+ psoe_leader +]'s caretaker committee announces the calendar: the new Secretary-General will be chosen by the members in a primary in May, and the 39th Federal Congress will meet in June to set the party's new leadership and programme. To stand, a candidate will need the endorsements of 5% of the membership, collected between 20 April and 4 May.

@lopez_announces
title: Patxi López announces
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: leadership_exception_open = 1 and calendar_seen = 1 and lopez_decided = 0 and sanchez_moderniser = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {! Q.lopez_decided = 1; Q.lopez_announce_time = Q.time; !}

= Patxi López announces

On 15 January, in Fuenlabrada, Patxi López announces that he will run for Secretary-General. He offers himself as the candidate who can unite the party: he stood with you in October, but he is no one's candidate but his own. Your people expect you to answer within days.

- @la_run: Announce your own candidacy, in Dos Hermanas, in Susana Díaz's own province
- @la_endorse: Endorse López: one candidate against Díaz, not two
- @la_conditions: Endorse López, on conditions
- @la_retire: Retire from politics

@la_run
subtitle: Three candidates: you, López and Díaz
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_backs_lopez = 0; Q.sanchismo += 4; Q.member_morale += 2; !}

On 28 January you announce your candidacy in Dos Hermanas, in the province of Seville. Everyone understands the gesture.

@la_endorse
subtitle: Most of your members follow you to López; if he wins, you are a backbencher in his party
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_backs_lopez = 1; Q.sanchismo -= 6; Q.rel_leadership = (Q.rel_leadership || 40) + 10; !}

You stand beside López in Madrid. Some of your volunteers cry; others start working for him the next morning.

@la_conditions
subtitle: López keeps "no es no" and gives you a place in his Executive if he wins; he may find the price too high
on-arrival: {! Q.lopez_accepts_terms = Math.random() < 0.7 ? 1 : 0; if (Q.lopez_accepts_terms) { Q.sanchez_backs_lopez = 2; Q.sanchismo -= 3; } else { Q.sanchez_backs_lopez = 0; Q.sanchismo += 2; } !}

[? if lopez_accepts_terms = 1 : López accepts: no abstention for the PP, ever again, and a seat in his Executive for you. You endorse him. ?][? if lopez_accepts_terms = 0 : López refuses: he will not be "Sánchez's candidate". You announce your own candidacy in Dos Hermanas on 28 January. ?]

@la_retire
subtitle: Ends your career
on-arrival: retired = 1

You announce that you are leaving politics. López and Díaz both praise your service.

@diaz_enters
title: Susana Díaz enters the race
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: leadership_exception_open = 1 and lopez_decided = 1 and diaz_entered = 0 and time >= lopez_announce_time + 2 and retired = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {! Q.diaz_entered = 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.primaryPoll(Q, 'signatures'); } !}

= Susana Díaz enters the race

On 12 March, in a packed pavilion in Madrid, Susana Díaz finally announces her candidacy. Felipe González, Zapatero and Alfonso Guerra are in the front row, with almost every regional baron. "I want to win," she says, "and I want to win for the PSOE." The old guard has its candidate.

The first polls of the endorsement race, taken among the party's office-holders and long-standing members: [+ ppoll_signatures +]. The pollsters reach the apparatus far more easily than the new members.

@endorsements
title: The endorsements
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: leadership_exception_open = 1 and diaz_entered = 1 and endorsements_done = 0 and ((year = 2017 and month >= 4) or year >= 2018)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.primaryEndorsements(Q); window.SpainGame.primaryPoll(Q, 'vote'); } else { Q.endorsements_done = 1; } !}
on-display: {!
if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.renderEndorsements(Q, 'sp-avales'); window.SpainGame.renderPollChange(Q, 'sp-avales-pollchange', 'endorsements'); }
!}

= The endorsements

From 20 April to 4 May the candidates collect the signed endorsements of the members: each needs 5% of the membership to stand. The federations' apparatus is good at this, and it shows.

{!<div id="sp-avales"></div>!}

{!<div id="sp-avales-pollchange"></div>!}

[+ av_leader +] wins the endorsements. [? if tapias_out = 1 : José Antonio Pérez Tapias falls short and is off the ballot. ?] Endorsements are not votes: in the secrecy of the ballot box, members can sign for one candidate and vote for another.

The polls for the vote on 21 May: [+ ppoll_vote +]. They have underrated insurgents before.

@iglesias_leaves
title: Pablo Iglesias leaves
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: iglesias_left = 0 and up_brand_exists = 1 and ((year = 2021 and month >= 3) or year >= 2022) and up_leader_is_iglesias = 1
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {! Q.iglesias_left = 1; Q.up_successor = window.SpainGame ? window.SpainGame.iglesiasSuccessor(Q) : 'Yolanda Díaz'; Q.succ_diaz = Q.up_successor === 'Yolanda Díaz' ? 1 : 0; Q.succ_montero = Q.up_successor === 'Irene Montero' ? 1 : 0; Q.up_in_govt = (Q.govt_parties || []).indexOf('up') !== -1 && !Q.acting ? 1 : 0; !}

= Pablo Iglesias leaves

[? if up_in_govt = 1 : Pablo Iglesias resigns as Second Deputy Prime Minister to run in the Madrid regional election against Isabel Díaz Ayuso. ?][? if up_in_govt = 0 : Pablo Iglesias announces that he will run in the Madrid regional election against Isabel Díaz Ayuso. ?] After a poor result in May he does what few expected: he leaves politics altogether, cuts off his ponytail, and goes back to the university and the media.

[? if succ_diaz = 1 : He has already named his successor: Yolanda Díaz, the Minister of Labour, a communist from Galicia whom even business leaders trust, and who gets on well with you. She will lead the space to the left of the PSOE, and soon she will want a platform of her own. ?][? if succ_montero = 1 : The succession goes to Irene Montero, his partner and the party's most combative voice. Podemos closes ranks and turns its fire on the PSOE. ?][? if succ_diaz = 0 : [? if succ_montero = 0 : Ione Belarra takes over Podemos, with Irene Montero at her side; Yolanda Díaz keeps her distance from the party's internal fights. ?] ?]

- @ig_praise: Praise Iglesias and welcome [+ up_successor +]
- @ig_court: Court the new leadership: offer a closer partnership
- @ig_poach: Go after his voters: "the useful vote on the left is the PSOE"

@ig_praise
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_up += 4; !}

A generous statement costs little.

@ig_court
subtitle: Closer relations with the left; the regional barons grumble
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_up += 10; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 3; !}

[+ up_successor +] takes the call.

@ig_poach
subtitle: Wins some of his voters; the new leadership will not forget it
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_up -= 10; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transferRaw(Q, 'up', 'psoe', { students: 1, workers: 1, professionals: 0.8 }); } !}

Some of his voters come home. His successor takes note.

@call_bluff
title: Call their bluff
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: bluff_due = 1 and bluff_seen = 0
on-arrival: {! Q.bluff_due = 0; Q.bluff_seen = 1; !}

= Call their bluff

The municipal elections have gone badly for the PSOE, and the PP is ready to govern town halls and regions with Vox[? if pp_vox_regions > 0 : , as it already does in [+ pp_vox_region_names +] ?]. Vox's vice-presidents are already cutting gender-violence programmes and talking about the Valley of the Fallen. The PP says the general election will be the same. Your team suggests something nobody expects: dissolve the Cortes now, and make the country choose before the summer.

- @bluff_snap: Call a snap general election: let the voters see what a PP-Vox Spain looks like
- @bluff_wait: Govern on until the end of the legislature

@bluff_snap
subtitle: The left mobilises behind the PSOE and the right has no time to settle; but you face the voters early
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.callElection(Q); window.SpainGame.transferRaw(Q, 'up', 'psoe', { students: 1.5, workers: 1.5, professionals: 1.2, unemployed: 1, pensioners: 0.8, homemakers: 0.8 }); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { pensioners: 1.2, workers: 1, professionals: 0.8, homemakers: 0.8, self_employed: 0.4 }); } Q.sanchismo += 6; Q.member_morale += 6; !}

The morning after the regional elections, you appear in the Moncloa and announce the dissolution of the Cortes. The PP, which expected six months to prepare, scrambles. On the left, everyone understands the question: you, or [+ pp_leader +] and Abascal.

@bluff_wait
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority -= 2; !}

You will finish the legislature. The PP spends the next months governing regions with Vox, and the photographs keep coming.

@labour_reform_vote
title: The labour reform vote
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: lr_vote_seen = 0 and psoe_in_government = 1 and sanchez_leader = 1 and acting = 0 and ((year = 2021 and month >= 12) or year >= 2022)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: lr_vote_seen = 1

= The labour reform vote

Yolanda Díaz's labour reform, agreed with the unions and the employers, comes to Congress: temporary contracts curbed, collective bargaining restored. ERC and Bildu say it does not go far enough; the PP votes no. It passes by a single vote, after a PP deputy presses the wrong button.

- @lr_celebrate: Celebrate the first labour reform in decades agreed by unions and employers
- @lr_credit: Share the credit with the social partners

@lr_celebrate
subtitle: Wins workers and the young; the unions approve
on-arrival: {! Q.trade_unionists_dissent -= 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { workers: 1.5, students: 1, unemployed: 1.2, professionals: 0.4 }); } !}

Permanent contracts start to rise within months.

@lr_credit
subtitle: Wins moderates; good relations with Podemos
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_up += 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { professionals: 0.8, self_employed: 0.6, workers: 0.6 }); } !}

Even the employers' association calls it a reasonable agreement.

@iberian_exception
title: The Iberian exception
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: iberian_seen = 0 and psoe_in_government = 1 and sanchez_leader = 1 and acting = 0 and ((year = 2022 and month >= 4) or year >= 2023)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: iberian_seen = 1

= The Iberian exception

With gas prices soaring after the invasion of Ukraine, Spain and Portugal win Brussels's permission to cap the price of gas used to generate electricity. Electricity bills fall while the rest of Europe's soar.

- @ib_families: Sell it as protecting families
- @ib_europe: Sell it as Spain leading in Europe

@ib_families
subtitle: Wins pensioners, families and workers
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { pensioners: 1.4, homemakers: 1.2, workers: 1, self_employed: 0.5 }); window.SpainGame.econ(Q, 0.1, -0.05); } !}

The bills arrive lower than last winter's.

@ib_europe
subtitle: Better relations with the EU and Portugal; wins professionals
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'eu', 4); window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'south', 4); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { professionals: 1, pensioners: 0.6 }); } !}

Others start to copy the idea.

@pensions_rise
title: Pensions rise with prices
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: pensions_rise_seen = 0 and psoe_in_government = 1 and sanchez_leader = 1 and acting = 0 and year >= 2023
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: pensions_rise_seen = 1

= Pensions rise with prices

In January, ten million pensions rise by 8.5%, in line with inflation, and the minimum wage reaches €1,080. The government says it promised and delivered.

- @pr_campaign: Make it the centre of the campaign
- @pr_quiet: Let the pay slips speak for themselves

@pr_campaign
subtitle: A big gain among pensioners and workers; Brussels watches the deficit
on-arrival: {! Q.fiscal_adj += 0.15; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { pensioners: 2.2, workers: 1.2, homemakers: 0.8 }); } !}

"Promises kept" is everywhere.

@pr_quiet
subtitle: A smaller gain, no extra spending
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { pensioners: 1.2, workers: 0.6 }); } !}

Pensioners notice anyway.

@eu_presidency
title: The EU presidency
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: eu_pres_seen = 0 and psoe_in_government = 1 and sanchez_leader = 1 and acting = 0 and ((year = 2023 and month >= 6) or year >= 2024)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: eu_pres_seen = 1

= The EU presidency

On 1 July Spain takes the rotating presidency of the Council of the European Union. For six months, Pedro Sánchez chairs Europe's agenda.

- @eup_statesman: Play the statesman at home and abroad
- @eup_focus: Keep it low-key: domestic politics first

@eup_statesman
subtitle: Better EU relations; wins moderates
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority += 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'eu', 5); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { professionals: 0.8, pensioners: 0.6, self_employed: 0.4 }); } !}

The photographs with Europe's leaders do their work.

@eup_focus
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'eu', 2); } !}

Brussels is efficient and unremarkable.

@local_elections
title: Municipal elections
new-page: true
