if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.renderLocal(Q, 'sp-local-result'); window.SpainGame.renderLocalMap(Q, 'sp-local-map'); window.SpainGame.renderPollChange(Q, 'sp-local-pollchange', 'local'); }
!}

= May [+ local_year +]: municipal elections

Spain elects its town and city councils. [+ local_winner +] wins the most councillors.

{!<div id="sp-local-result"></div>!}

{!<div id="sp-local-map"></div>!}

{!<div id="sp-local-pollchange"></div>!}

[? if local_poor = 1 : It is a bad night for the PSOE[? if local_psoe_change < 0 : : it loses [+ local_psoe_change +] councillors ?], and the town halls it loses are the ones that organise its campaigns. ?][? if local_poor = 0 : The PSOE holds its ground in the town halls. ?]

@realignment
title: A realignment
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: realign_due = 1
on-arrival: realign_due = 0

= [+ realign_name +] overtakes [+ realign_old +]

[? if realign_right = 1 : For two years [+ realign_name +] has polled ahead of [+ realign_old +]. Donors, mayors and commentators start to treat it as the main party of the Spanish right. [+ realign_old +] does not collapse overnight, but from now on its voters drift away month after month. ?][? if realign_psoe_lost = 1 : The sorpasso has happened, and it has lasted: [+ realign_name +] has polled ahead of the PSOE for two years. For the first time since 1977 the PSOE is not the main party of the Spanish left, and every month more of its voters follow the new leader. ?][? if realign_psoe_back = 1 : The PSOE is back: it has polled ahead of [+ realign_old +] for two years, and the left's voters drift home. ?][? if realign_left_other = 1 : [+ realign_name +] has overtaken [+ realign_old +] for good on the left. ?][? if realign_iu = 1 : Izquierda Unida has polled ahead of Podemos for a year and a half. The old communist-led coalition takes back its place as the main radical left party, and Podemos's voters begin to drift to it. ?][? if realign_up_back = 1 : Podemos has polled ahead of Izquierda Unida for a year and a half, and takes back its place as the main radical left party. ?]

[+ realign_name +] is now the leading party of its camp.

@begona_case
title: Five days of reflection
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: begona_seen = 0 and sanchez_pm = 1 and ((year = 2024 and month >= 4) or year >= 2025)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: begona_seen = 1

= Five days of reflection

A Madrid judge opens an investigation into Begoña Gómez, your wife, on a complaint from Manos Limpias based on press cuttings. Within months your brother David's job at the Badajoz provincial council is also before a judge. The right speaks of a corrupt family; your supporters speak of lawfare.

- @begona_reflect: Withdraw for five days to decide whether it is worth it
- @begona_fight: Say nothing and keep governing

@begona_reflect
title: The letter to the citizens
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchismo += 8; Q.member_morale += 6; Q.sanchez_authority += 4; Q.rel_pp -= 6; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { workers: 0.5, students: 0.5, pensioners: 0.3 }); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'pp', { professionals: 0.3, self_employed: 0.3 }); } !}

Thousands rally outside Ferraz asking you to stay. On the fifth day you stay. Your opponents call it theatre; your voters call it dignity. The cases continue.

@begona_fight
title: Governing through it
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority -= 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { workers: -0.2, professionals: -0.2, pensioners: -0.2, self_employed: -0.2, students: -0.2, unemployed: -0.2, homemakers: -0.2 }); } !}

The headlines keep coming, week after week.

@koldo_case
title: The Koldo case
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: koldo_seen = 0 and psoe_in_government = 1 and sanchez_leader = 1 and year >= 2024
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {! Q.koldo_seen = 1; Q.abalos_gone = 1; Q.adv_cerdan_was = Q.adv_cerdan; Q.adv_cerdan = 0; Q.adv_offer_cerdan = 0; Q.sanchez_authority -= 6; Q.member_morale -= 6; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { workers: -0.7, professionals: -0.7, pensioners: -0.7, self_employed: -0.7, students: -0.7, unemployed: -0.7, homemakers: -0.7 }); } !}

= The Koldo case

Masks bought at the height of the pandemic, commissions, a former bodyguard turned adviser: the Civil Guard's reports on Koldo García reach José Luis Ábalos, your old Minister of Transport and organisation secretary, who is expelled from the group and later jailed pending trial. Then, in June 2025, a recording reaches Santos Cerdán, the man who collected the signatures for your comeback. He resigns as Secretary of Organisation the same day.[? if adv_cerdan_was = 1 : Cerdán was on your team. Every photograph of the two of you is on the front pages. ?]

- @koldo_sorry: Ask forgiveness and order an external audit
- @koldo_deny: Call it a conspiracy

@koldo_sorry
title: Forgiveness
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority += 2; Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { professionals: 0.3, pensioners: 0.2 }); } !}

"I trusted the wrong people." It hurts, and it is believed by more people than you feared.

@koldo_deny
title: A conspiracy
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchismo += 3; Q.modernisers_dissent += 5; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 5; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { professionals: -0.5, self_employed: -0.3 }); } !}

The base believes you. Almost nobody else does.

