= The DANA

On 29 October 2024 a cut-off low dumps a year's rain on the south of Valencia in a few hours. More than two hundred people die in Paiporta, Catarroja, Sedaví. The regional alert reaches phones when the water is already in the garages. In Paiporta, the King, the Valencian president and [? if sanchez_pm = 1 : you ?][? if sanchez_pm = 0 : the Prime Minister ?] are pelted with mud.

- @dana_central: [? if sanchez_pm = 1 : Declare a national emergency and take command ?][? if sanchez_pm = 0 : Demand that the State take command ?]
- @dana_support: [? if sanchez_pm = 1 : "If they need help, let them ask for it": support the regional government ?][? if sanchez_pm = 0 : Support the relief effort quietly ?]

@dana_central
title: The State takes command
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority += 3; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { pensioners: 0.4, workers: 0.4 }); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'pp', { pensioners: -0.4, workers: -0.3 }); } !}

Soldiers, engineers and money arrive at once. The Valencian government is blamed for its silence that afternoon.

@dana_support
title: A shared failure
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { pensioners: -0.3, workers: -0.3 }); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'pp', { pensioners: -0.4 }); window.SpainGame.voxFlow(Q, 0.4); } !}

Every administration blames another. Vox blames all of them, and grows.

