= The last autumn of the legislature

Without budgets since 2023, without Junts, with your Secretary of Organisation in court, the legislature is exhausted. The Constitution gives you until the summer of 2027.

- @diss_now: Dissolve the Cortes: a general election on 29 November
- @diss_wait: Hold on into 2027

@diss_now
title: Dissolution
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.callElection(Q); } Q.election_month = 11; Q.member_morale += 3; !}

The decree appears in the Boletín Oficial del Estado the next morning. The campaign begins.

@diss_wait
title: Holding on
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority -= 3; !}

You will govern until the last possible day.

@psc_breaks
title: The PSC breaks with the PSOE
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: psc_due = 1
on-arrival: psc_due = 0

= The PSC breaks with the PSOE

[? if grand_coalition = 1 : A grand coalition with the PP ?][? if grand_coalition = 0 : The PSOE's line on Catalonia ?] was too much for Catalonia's socialists. The National Council of the PSC votes to end the 1978 protocol that bound it to the PSOE. Its [+ psc_moved_congress +] deputies form their own group in Congress, its senators and its MEP follow, and its deputies in the Parliament of Catalonia and its town councillors now answer only to the PSC.

The PSC will not merge with ERC: it is federalist, not independentist, and its voters in the industrial belt of Barcelona are the least nationalist in Catalonia. It stays a party of its own, closer to the Comuns than to anyone in Madrid.

The PSOE must now decide whether to run its own candidates in Catalonia.

- @psc_run: Found PSOE-Cat and run against the PSC
- @psc_pact: No lists in Catalonia: a pact with the PSC

@psc_run
title: PSOE-Cat
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.pscChoice(Q, 1); } Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 5; Q.progressives_dissent += 5; !}

The PSOE founds its own federation in Catalonia. It will win some unionist voters the PSC has lost, but every seat it takes comes from the PSC, and the PSC's deputies will not vote for you lightly.

@psc_pact
title: A pact with the PSC
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.pscChoice(Q, 0); } Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 3; !}

The PSOE leaves Catalonia to the PSC. In return, the PSC's deputies will usually vote with you in Congress, as a separate group.

