= The Senate veto is lifted

Two months after the Senate vetoed it, Congress lifts the veto on the [+ senate_lifted +]. It finally comes into force.

@alt_history
title: History takes another turn
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: alt_due = 1
on-arrival: alt_due = 0

= [? if alt_errejon = 1 : Errejón wins Vistalegre II ?][? if alt_vox_ortega = 1 : Ortega Smith takes over Vox ?][? if alt_vox_espinosa = 1 : Espinosa de los Monteros takes over Vox ?][? if alt_cat_talks = 1 : Rajoy sits down with Puigdemont ?][? if alt_iceta = 1 : Iceta's surge ?]

[? if alt_errejon = 1 : At Podemos's second assembly, Íñigo Errejón's line beats Pablo Iglesias's. Podemos will seek transversal voters and talk to the PSOE rather than try to replace it. Iglesias stays as a deputy; his supporters drift towards Izquierda Unida. ?][? if alt_vox_ortega = 1 : Santiago Abascal steps back and Javier Ortega Smith takes over Vox: harder, more confrontational, aimed at working-class neighbourhoods rather than at disappointed PP voters. ?][? if alt_vox_espinosa = 1 : Iván Espinosa de los Monteros takes over Vox and turns it towards economic liberalism: low taxes, less state. It wins over business-minded Ciudadanos voters and loses some workers. ?][? if alt_cat_talks = 1 : Instead of Article 155, Mariano Rajoy opens secret talks with the Generalitat through the Basque nationalists. There is no direct rule, no declaration of independence, and no prison for the Catalan leaders. The right calls it surrender; Vox grows on it. ?][? if alt_iceta = 1 : Miquel Iceta's campaign catches fire: dancing on stage, promising pardons and a federal Spain, he wins the unionist vote that in history went to Ciudadanos. ?]
